1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
You

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:09,440
I'm growing tired of it, so I'm putting an end to you now

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Hinokami Kagura

4
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:18,440
Raging Sun

5
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:27,200
Flame dance that was underwhelming but

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
He's gone?

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Hinokami Kagura! Fake Rainbow!

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,000
I can do this!

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Hinokami Kagura! Firewheel!

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Firewheel!

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Firewheel!

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Firewheel!

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Quickly! Recovery! Breathing!

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Firewheel!

15
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Firewheel!

16
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
I can do this! I can take on an upper rank demon!

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,380
I can do this. I can take on an upper-ranked demon!

18
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:14,980
I can take on an upper-ranked demon.

19
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:44,980
I can take on an upper-ranked demon.

20
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:14,980
I can take on an upper-ranked demon.

21
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:44,960
I can take on an upper-ranked demon.

22
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:49,920
No. It's more like the ones that were split off are now returning to her.

23
00:03:49,920 --> 00:04:00,740
Stand your ground. Get your breathing under control.

24
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:02,900
And strike!

25
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,720
I knew it.

26
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:07,020
She's gone!

27
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:10,640
It seems I was right.

28
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:14,980
Hashira really did show up!

29
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,060
How magnificent!

30
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:20,640
I can't even imagine how pleased my master will be!

31
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:23,500
She just transformed.

32
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:26,920
Her scent couldn't be more ominous.

33
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:29,320
It's making me sick already.

34
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:32,660
Which means she gained even more power.

35
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:39,220
But if Mr. Uzui really is with Inosuke and the others right now, then I can rest easy.

36
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,300
Keep it down out there, will ya?

37
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:44,180
Is that a sword in your head, kid?

38
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:48,060
You've got a lot of nerve-picking fights out in front of my house.

39
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:49,980
What kind of mischief is this?

40
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:52,500
We made too much noise and now people are in danger.

41
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:58,300
I'll have you know that this Hanamachi is only viable because we and our clients all follow the rules.

42
00:04:58,780 --> 00:05:01,580
So if you're gonna cause trouble, you're not welcome here.

43
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:03,620
Get the hell out of my sight!

44
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:06,520
You should keep your mouth shut.

45
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:12,620
This is bad.

46
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,180
Please, sir, don't come this way!

47
00:05:15,380 --> 00:05:15,660
Huh?

48
00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:17,360
Stay back, please!

49
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:23,860
It's too dangerous! Get back inside!

50
00:05:23,860 --> 00:05:24,280
Get back inside!

51
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:49,360
Aro, please! Get up! We have to run! We have to run!

52
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:51,680
Stay calm.

53
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,400
Sir, you're going to survive this.

54
00:05:55,860 --> 00:05:56,660
But your arm.

55
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:58,900
You need to stop the bleeding.

56
00:05:58,900 --> 00:05:58,980
Aro, please!

57
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:00,980
Get up! We have to run! We have to run!

58
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:03,660
Stay calm.

59
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:05,360
Sir, you're going to survive this.

60
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:06,500
But your arm.

61
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:07,840
Get back here.

62
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:11,140
I won't let you get away with this!

63
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:12,900
Not after what you just did!

64
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:14,860
What's wrong?

65
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,740
You still have something to say?

66
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:20,220
Your efforts are useless and you're hideous.

67
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:23,960
There's no reason to let ugly people like yourself live.

68
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:27,060
So do us a favor and die alongside them.

69
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:33,580
Aro, wake up!

70
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:34,840
We have to leave!

71
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:35,980
Help us!

72
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:37,320
Somebody help us, please!

73
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:37,900
Somebody help us, please!

74
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,960
Everyone get back inside!

75
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:43,320
It's too dangerous to stay out here!

76
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:56,100
Dear Kamado, I know now that I wronged you.

77
00:06:56,100 --> 00:07:02,140
Thank you for shedding the tears I couldn't over my son, Kyojuro.

78
00:07:02,140 --> 00:07:12,100
And if I'm not mistaken, you've been exchanging letters with Senjuro for the past four months or so.

79
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:16,420
He seems to be in a much better place now.

80
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:23,000
I'm horribly ashamed that our first meeting went the way that it did.

81
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:31,940
At a time when my own incompetence had left me shattered, things went from bad to worse when my beloved wife succumbed to illness.

82
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:37,780
Since then, I've done nothing but drink myself into a stupor and wallow.

83
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:40,340
I've been a useless father.

84
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:47,040
Thankfully, Kyojuro somehow turned out to be a fine son.

85
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:56,420
Even after I abandoned him as an instructor and a father, he pushed forward studying the guide to flame breathing and became a Hashira.

86
00:07:56,420 --> 00:08:05,380
Although there are only three volumes, he must have more of his mother, Luka's blood in him.

87
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:10,660
Both Kyojuro and Senjuro are fine boys.

88
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:16,860
But Kamado, you are just as exceptional, if not more, young man.

89
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:26,120
Rumor has it that those who are chosen to wield sun-breathing are born with the same red mark on their forehead that you have.

90
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:29,560
So I'm sure that you will.

91
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:33,180
No, you're wrong, Mr. Shinjiro.

92
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:36,200
I wasn't born with this scar to begin with.

93
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:42,560
Originally, it was just a burn mark from when I protected my younger brother from a falling brazier.

94
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:49,000
After that, I was injured during final selection, which is how it ended up the way it is now.

95
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:55,780
I was told that my father was born with a faint mark on his forehead, but that wasn't the case with me.

96
00:08:57,380 --> 00:09:01,360
Which means I must not be one of the chosen wielders that you're talking about.

97
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:07,200
But that doesn't matter right now.

98
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:17,560
Even if I'm not one of the chosen ones, even if I'm not up to the task, there are times like this where I can't just back down.

99
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:22,760
Because in this world, there are those that lack any trace of a human heart.

100
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:28,920
Killing innocent people without any hesitation, and moving on without any regret.

101
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:38,080
She is that kind of evil, but as long as I live, I won't allow it!

102
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:45,900
Those lost lives will never return!

103
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:49,120
They can't just regenerate!

104
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:54,380
That's a luxury only demons have!

105
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,180
Why do you kill?

106
00:09:57,840 --> 00:10:00,000
Why trample over the lives of the innocent?

107
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,760
I feel like I've heard these same words before.

108
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:09,860
Such disregard for human life. What's so amusing about this?

109
00:10:11,060 --> 00:10:14,660
So tell me then, what is the weight of a human life to you?

110
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:17,500
Wait, who was that?

111
00:10:18,380 --> 00:10:20,120
Why can't you understand?

112
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:23,520
How could you ever forget?

113
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,440
Something's not right.

114
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,400
I don't remember this.

115
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,900
These aren't my memories at all.

116
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:33,500
It must be the cells.

117
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:36,960
They're Lord Muzan's memories.

118
00:10:36,960 --> 00:11:06,940
They're Lord Muzan's memories.

119
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:11,000
I saved everyone who was trapped in here, so what's the issue?

120
00:11:11,860 --> 00:11:14,300
You should be on your knees worshipping me right now.

121
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:16,360
We'll talk about the other thing later.

122
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:20,620
Lord Tengen, if you don't go after it, there'll be even more bloodshed.

123
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:23,460
Don't worry about us and get over there before it's too late.

124
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,440
You heard what they said.

125
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:30,660
Get ready. We're giving chase.

126
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,280
Take out the base, boys.

127
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:39,520
Get out of my way, because Lord Tengen is coming through.

128
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:44,740
How the hell is he so fast?

129
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:51,380
What is it? Spit it out.

130
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:54,860
You were once a human. Isn't that right?

131
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:59,280
Which means you shed tears and suffered like any other normal human would.

132
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,640
Just when I thought you couldn't get any more annoying.

133
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:06,520
Luckily, I don't remember anything about the past.

134
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:09,760
I'm a demon now, so who cares about my human past?

135
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,920
Life is better like this.

136
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:15,060
Us demons don't have to buy food or grow old.

137
00:12:15,060 --> 00:12:17,780
Or get sick or die.

138
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:21,060
We have nothing to lose.

139
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:24,060
Not to mention...

140
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:28,740
Beautiful, powerful demons can do anything we want!

141
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:37,280
Blood demon art!

142
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:42,960
Eight lair to obi-slash!

143
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:47,880
Let's see how an idiot like you stops an attack like this.

144
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:50,960
A crossblow leaving you with nowhere to run.

145
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:55,600
Using the parts of my body that were split off to take control of this area.

146
00:12:56,360 --> 00:13:00,020
Now that I'm whole again, my speed is in a class of its own.

147
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:05,500
Seeing as you could barely hold your own against my non-blood demon art, it's all over for you.

148
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:10,980
So, hideous boy, I'm going to cut you and that decrepit sword into pieces.

149
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:17,340
Now then, I'll be making my way to that Hashira!

150
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:22,680
Hinokami Kagura, Burning Bones, Summer Sun.

151
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:27,820
This pain! What just happened?

152
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:31,940
It feels like I've just suffered burns where I received that slash!

153
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:34,380
Which means I can't regenerate!

154
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:36,600
But his wounds must be deep too!

155
00:13:37,800 --> 00:13:41,880
Making such violent motions should have instantly ruptured everything within his body!

156
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:47,940
What? How is he able to slice my belt?

157
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:51,120
Something's not right here!

158
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:54,560
My fingertips are trembling?

159
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:56,360
This isn't like me!

160
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:58,940
Lord Muzan!

161
00:13:58,940 --> 00:14:03,940
Damn it!

162
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:05,780
Why is he faster than before?

163
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,980
None of this makes any sense!

164
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:09,600
Don't you feel any pain?

165
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:11,240
Are you human?

166
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:11,340
Are you human?

167
00:14:11,340 --> 00:14:24,840
As if someone like you could ever hope to decapitate a demon as strong as me!

168
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:29,100
It's soft.

169
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:31,180
Too soft for me to cut through.

170
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:34,240
It was able to blunt my slash by bending.

171
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:37,820
I won't let you get away!

172
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:38,860
You hideous!

173
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:40,060
Why are you dumb?

174
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:42,720
There are more belts now.

175
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:44,100
Thirteen of them.

176
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,220
If I dodge them, they might wreak even more havoc.

177
00:14:48,760 --> 00:14:50,240
But for some reason...

178
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:53,360
They're moving so slowly.

179
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:56,340
Just try and cut me now!

180
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:57,120
You can't!

181
00:14:57,560 --> 00:15:00,340
That last exchange of ours was nothing more than a fluke!

182
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:06,360
What?

183
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:09,080
He gathered all of my belts in one spot!

184
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:14,120
You think that's enough to stop me?

185
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:16,340
It'll take more than that!

186
00:15:16,340 --> 00:15:21,060
You might be able to pull them tight enough to cut through.

187
00:15:21,780 --> 00:15:24,680
But I can loosen them all again in the blink of an eye.

188
00:15:25,780 --> 00:15:29,340
So unless you can close the distance between us faster than that, you...

189
00:15:29,340 --> 00:15:30,340
What?

190
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:37,400
He slashed them!

191
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:39,120
He's fast!

192
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,140
It's simple, really.

193
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:45,220
I just had to bring my sword down faster than they could start bending.

194
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:48,300
I can decapitate her this time.

195
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:49,620
It's over.

196
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:51,780
Brother, please!

197
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:57,340
Brother, please!

198
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:58,460
You have to breathe!

199
00:15:58,680 --> 00:15:59,000
Hurry!

200
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:17,400
You humans never cease to amaze me with how pathetic you all are.

201
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:22,760
If that really was the best you could do, then I might actually be starting to feel a little bit bad for you.

202
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:25,000
I can't stop coughing.

203
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:26,880
It's so hard...

204
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:27,520
To breathe!

205
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:31,460
Which means I must have gone well beyond my stamina threshold.

206
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,540
My vision's going dark.

207
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:37,680
All I can hear is the sound of my heartbeat.

208
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:43,220
Since you're human, I'm afraid your wounds won't be healing anytime soon.

209
00:16:43,900 --> 00:16:45,340
Blame your own flesh and blood.

210
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:49,000
Stand up.

211
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:50,400
Wield your sword.

212
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:55,260
But I'll do you a favor, and show you how to decapitate your enemy!

213
00:16:55,260 --> 00:16:55,980
Hey!

214
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:27,880
You have some nerve doing that!

215
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:32,820
Wait a second. That filthy traitor. It's you, isn't it?

216
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:35,580
The one he was talking about has to be you!

217
00:17:38,620 --> 00:17:43,180
Daki. There's a demon out there that managed to slip from my grasp.

218
00:17:43,780 --> 00:17:45,120
Just as Tamayo did.

219
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:48,740
I need you to find and dispose of her.

220
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:51,280
You're the only one I can turn to.

221
00:17:52,540 --> 00:17:54,760
It shouldn't be hard to recognize her.

222
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:58,560
She's a girl clad in a hemp-leaf-patterned kimono and a checkered belt.

223
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:06,780
Lord Muzan!

224
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:10,200
I will happily eviscerate this hideous little runt!

225
00:18:10,540 --> 00:18:11,720
Prepare to die, scum!

226
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:21,760
Is chicken the only thing you know?!

227
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:25,340
You've got to beat her!

228
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:37,600
Could you be any weaker?

229
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,840
You've barely consumed any humans.

230
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:43,380
It's a miracle you were able to escape Lord Muzan.

231
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:46,560
Aw, you poor thing.

232
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:50,120
Your torso and lower body went their separate ways.

233
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:52,480
I wouldn't try moving if I were you.

234
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:59,340
After all, there's no way a half-developed demon like yourself could possibly regenerate quickly enough to continue fighting.

235
00:18:59,340 --> 00:19:04,120
But since we're both demons, I'll quit toying around with you.

236
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:08,580
And instead, I'll absorb you into my belt and expose you to the sun in the morning.

237
00:19:09,620 --> 00:19:13,680
Like I'd waste my time finishing you off when I have a Hashira to kill.

238
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:22,720
What's going on?

239
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:25,200
She's regenerated her leg.

240
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,320
Never mind her leg.

241
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:28,800
How is she able to stand?

242
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:32,640
I'm sure I severed her in half.

243
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:35,220
I saw it with my own eyes.

244
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:36,740
There's no way I missed!

245
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:45,240
I didn't expect this.

246
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:49,500
Her healing and regeneration speed is on par with upper-ranked demons.

247
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:11,940
What is this intimidating presence that's radiating from her?

248
00:20:12,980 --> 00:20:14,840
Her whole demeanor's changed.

249
00:20:22,020 --> 00:20:22,580
Brother...

250
00:20:22,580 --> 00:20:26,280
You and Sister sure do take after one another.

251
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:31,080
You're gentle, but scary when you get mad.

252
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:39,740
Like Sister, when that scary grown-up bumped into a kid and hurt him, she got in his face, demanding he apologize.

253
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:46,360
I mean, luckily there were tons of adults around, but...

254
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:48,540
It still made me nervous.

255
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:54,900
People who get mad at others don't tend to have any regard for their own safety.

256
